  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Concentrations"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "A Concentration is a Senate-approved curricular element that provides students the opportunity to develop in-depth knowledge representing a sub-specialization or emphasis within the core of a degree program or major. Courses for a Concentration are selected from the core elective courses offered to students within their degree program or major. Concentrations are optional."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "For more information see Senate Policy 2 (opens in new window) , Section 7.1 Concentration",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Senate Policy 2 (opens in new window)",
          "url": "https://www.torontomu.ca/content/ryerson/senate/policies/undergraduate-curriculum-structure-policy-2/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Policy Elements"
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "A Concentration curriculum consists of at least six, specified/prescribed one- term degree-level core elective courses offered to students within their degree program or major."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Core required courses of the degree program or major may not be included in the course count/defined structure of a Concentration."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "The completion of a Concentration cannot be made mandatory."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Earning one Concentration will not increase the number of courses required to graduate."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Where it is possible, a student may complete more than one Concentration; however, no individual course can be applied to satisfy the requirements of more than one Concentration."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Course substitutions are not permitted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Completion of a Concentration is subject to availability of courses."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Completion of the degree, with the addition of more than one Concentration, may require the completion of extra courses. Additional fees may also be incurred."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Students must complete all courses in a Concentration prior to graduation from their program of studies."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Restrictions [e.g., grade variations on individual courses; a minimum Cumulative Grade Point Average (CGPA) requirement for completion of the Concentration] are not permitted."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Any course used to satisfy a requirement of a Concentration cannot also be used to satisfy a requirement of a Minor."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Students must declare a Concentration(s) at a time specified by their program."
    },
    {
      "kind": "list_item",
      "text": "Completion of a Concentration is noted on the academic transcript, but not on the award document."
    },
